{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas","id":1070604,"title":"Perfected Material Ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T06:23:14-07:00","id":1070604,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Perfected Material Ideas","content":"I recently started in a game and am playing someone trying to make it into the fashion field. So my ST, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar728_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"728\" data-vbnamecard=\"728\">CrownedSun</a> , had linked me to the preview of perfected materials since that sort of thing suits me. I like playing crafters, and there are imperial brocades that use threads of precious metals.<br /> <br /> Anyways, what really caught my eye was alkahest or perfected water. It dissolves things, which could be incredibly useful. The first thing I thought of was this could let you potentially merge materials in ways that wouldn't happen naturally by dissolving them then evaporating the water (since I assume that's possible with effort). Say a sheet of lapis lazuli infused silk, where the particles of stone are entangled up in the proteins of the silk. But you could take it further... what about metal and say... wood.<br /> <br /> I feel like the potential here is pretty significant, and while I've focused on water, I've only started scratching the surface. What ideas do other people have?<br /> <br /> Oh, and I had the vague idea that you could perfect plants and other living materials, to serve as part of decorating a ritual space. But that was more a side thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:02:06-07:00","id":1070616,"title":"","content":"I don't know if evaporating the alkahest would be a good idea since you'd have water vapor that could dissolve anything floating around unless you contained it with magic (Then again you need magic to contain it anyway), but its kind of a moot point anyway since Matter could just extract the particulate perfected materials anyway.<br /> <br /> Cool idea fusing it to other materials though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T07:06:26-07:00","id":1070617,"title":"","content":"I had thought about that, and anyways, waste not, want not. I figured you'd do something like a still, to recollect the alkahest once evaporated. On the other hand, as long as you didn't make it forever perfected, it might not be that much of an issue as vapor. But good point at using Matter to extract the materials!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T08:42:05-07:00","id":1070674,"title":"","content":"You could also use alkahest to create mundane super alloys without all the special tooling/labor/etc. It would be a very profitable business venture for a mage.<br /> <br /> For fun I looked up the rough values for some metals. Gamma Ti-Al a superalloy for jet engines is worth roughly 20 million US dollars per metric tonne (I'm scaling up from an estimate from a NASA white paper). The raw material costs would be roughly eight thousand dollars per tonne. So yeah, make the Moros pay for dinner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12298,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","user":"Enlightened_Milkman","date":".  rough napkin math 03-30-2017, 05:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12298-enlightened_milkman","name":"Enlightened_Milkman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T18:41:21-07:00","id":1070972,"title":"","content":"I don't know if Alkahest would evaporate and leave behind what you are looking for. It would be like a residue or something right? A single medium? How do you get the lapiz lazuli silk back into threads or fibers? It sounds like it would end up like lint does in the pockets of your pants after the washing and drying of laundry.<br /> <br /> Do you have access to Promethean or Changeling? If you have any crossover potential, exotic alchemy or exotic fibres and materials might be possible with those games. Hedgespun fibres can be made from exotic stuff like starlight and tears, but appears as gorgeous, but still mundane, fibres to anyone else.<br /> <br /> But I definitely see what you are going for. The others mentioned just using Matter spells themselves, but you're looking for something that withstands scrutiny and doesn't fall apart to sleeper disbelief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T20:30:34-07:00","id":1071005,"title":"","content":"I was thinking it'd make a sheet, not woven. The question at that point is &quot;what does a sheet of silk without threads look/feel/act like?&quot; Which in the end, I think, requires ST thoughts on what it means. I just think the idea is fascinating, and my fashion mage would want to at least CHECK what the results were. And if it wouldn't provide any results she was happy with, then that opens up the door to new experiments! And in the end, isn't discovery part of the wonder of Mage? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:12:46-07:00","id":1071056,"title":"","content":"Silk is a polymer. Perfect forms would presumably not have weird perturbations and so be perfect strands. Possibly, then, one perfect strand.<br /> This could wend all over itself and be felt-like, or simply wander through your material as a strand.<br /> Less chemical perfection, on the other hand, could mean that it is a handful of strands, so, again, be essentially a felt.<br /> In any of these cases, it would <i>tend</i> towards <b>really thin</b>.<br /> <br /> That's my quick thoughts on that part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:28:22-07:00","id":1071067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071005#post1071005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking it'd make a sheet, not woven. The question at that point is &quot;what does a sheet of silk without threads look/feel/act like?&quot; Which in the end, I think, requires ST thoughts on what it means. I just think the idea is fascinating, and my fashion mage would want to at least CHECK what the results were. And if it wouldn't provide any results she was happy with, then that opens up the door to new experiments! And in the end, isn't discovery part of the wonder of Mage? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do love magical experiments!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T01:16:13-07:00","id":1071118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enlightened_Milkman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1070674#post1070674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could also use alkahest to create mundane super alloys without all the special tooling/labor/etc. It would be a very profitable business venture for a mage.<br /> <br /> For fun I looked up the rough values for some metals. Gamma Ti-Al a superalloy for jet engines is worth roughly 20 million US dollars per metric tonne (I'm scaling up from an estimate from a NASA white paper). The raw material costs would be roughly eight thousand dollars per tonne. So yeah, make the Moros pay for dinner.</div> </div> </div> </div>This... does not work that way. To make a superalloy out of titanium and aluminium you need to melt them together and cool them in a very specific way so that you get two differend mixed crystals of materials bonded together. Dissolving does kind of the oposite, it breaks every bonding of materials appart and leaves very tiny part up to single atoms or molecules floating around in the solvent. So if you mix titanium and aluminium in Alkahest and vaporize it afterwards, all you would get is very fine aluminium and titanium powder.<br /> <br /> Same goes for silk or minerals. If you put silk or a diamond into a perfect solvent, all you would get in the end is carbon powder. What you could do is make extremely fine powders out of raw elements like gold or platinum and then use a simple mater spell to weave these into a silk thread for example. And that silk could likely be perfected in any other way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T01:38:51-07:00","id":1071124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071118#post1071118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This... does not work that way. To make a superalloy out of titanium and aluminium you need to melt them together and cool them in a very specific way so that you get two differend mixed crystals of materials bonded together. Dissolving does kind of the oposite, it breaks every bonding of materials appart and leaves very tiny part up to single atoms or molecules floating around in the solvent. So if you mix titanium and aluminium in Alkahest and vaporize it afterwards, all you would get is very fine aluminium and titanium powder.<br /> <br /> Same goes for silk or minerals. If you put silk or a diamond into a perfect solvent, all you would get in the end is carbon powder. What you could do is make extremely fine powders out of raw elements like gold or platinum and then use a simple mater spell to weave these into a silk thread for example. And that silk could likely be perfected in any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wouldn't stand up to Quiescence for long would it?<br /> <br /> <br /> I am thinking a Legacy surrounding this would be the best thing to go for. Gosh the money you could make, and it probably won't get you in huge trouble like a lot of other &quot;miracle&quot; legacies would!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T02:55:01-07:00","id":1071148,"title":"","content":"I don't see any problems with Quiescence honestly. You can also get very fine powders in other ways, at the very least theoretically, so there is nothing &quot;physically weird&quot; about silkthreads with gold particals, it just would be a lot more expensive to do it without magic. I'm just saying that you cannot use a dissolving process to combine stuff. That would be like to create a really cold fire or a very bright shadow. It just makes logically no sense even with magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T03:07:02-07:00","id":1071155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071148#post1071148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be like to create a really cold fire or a very bright shadow. It just makes logically no sense even with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't tell me what I can or can't do with my magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It makes perfect sense to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T03:17:00-07:00","id":1071159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071148#post1071148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see any problems with Quiescence honestly. You can also get very fine powders in other ways, at the very least theoretically, so there is nothing &quot;physically weird&quot; about silkthreads with gold particals, it just would be a lot more expensive to do it without magic. I'm just saying that you cannot use a dissolving process to combine stuff. That would be like to create a really cold fire or a very bright shadow. It just makes logically no sense even with magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, put that way it probably would--especially if the ST allows the effect to be Lasting... which given Matter spells it probably already is!<br /> <br /> Actually if OP wants to go with perfected materials specifically, the alkahest could be used to make powders, and the powders could be mixed with mundane water and converted into Perfected Dyes mayhaps, and then <i>that</i> could do something interesting afterwards...!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T03:18:29-07:00","id":1071160,"title":"","content":"Perfected Glass is NASTY stuff.<br /> Harden it with Alter Integrity, and you can quickly and easily make extremely dangerous traps, which monsters will quite literally run themselves onto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:12:24-07:00","id":1071210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071118#post1071118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This... does not work that way. To make a superalloy out of titanium and aluminium you need to melt them together and cool them in a very specific way so that you get two differend mixed crystals of materials bonded together. Dissolving does kind of the oposite, it breaks every bonding of materials appart and leaves very tiny part up to single atoms or molecules floating around in the solvent. So if you mix titanium and aluminium in Alkahest and vaporize it afterwards, all you would get is very fine aluminium and titanium powder.<br /> <br /> Same goes for silk or minerals. If you put silk or a diamond into a perfect solvent, all you would get in the end is carbon powder. What you could do is make extremely fine powders out of raw elements like gold or platinum and then use a simple mater spell to weave these into a silk thread for example. And that silk could likely be perfected in any other way.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing to remember is that, with water, the speed at which the state change takes place matters. There's a reason why cryopreservation of cells is done by freezing them very quickly (along with other things such as DMSO, but I digress). The reason is that crystal formation is prevented except at the smallest possible way. There's ice, but the crystals are SMALL. By comparison, if you slowly freeze water, the ice crystals will be much larger.<br /> <br /> Proteins are regularly dissolved in water. We can produce silk like polymers already through techniques, though thinking about it, doing what I'm talking about with silk might require similar, specialized equipment to produce threads, but we're talking a sheet and the polymers are going to be already prone to forming a polymer (though it might require enzymes to catalyze the reaction). I've worked with proteins a LOT in research labs. Polymers less so, but I know more than the basics.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you can have long strands of biological material dissolved in water. That's what DNA is, it's not a short molecule, but a very long one. And the labs I worked in were dealing with both DNA and long protein molecules, cut to single genes, but they're still very tiny on some scales... just not as tiny as singular atoms or simple sugars.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: This came off more aggressive than I meant it. I stand by what I said, BUT... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11939\" data-vbnamecard=\"11939\">HardcoreHannes</a> brought up some points which did make me think about it in ways that'd make it more reasonable to make a sheet (namely the enzymes being added).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 03-31-2017, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:15:03-07:00","id":1071213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071159#post1071159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, put that way it probably would--especially if the ST allows the effect to be Lasting... which given Matter spells it probably already is!<br /> <br /> Actually if OP wants to go with perfected materials specifically, the alkahest could be used to make powders, and the powders could be mixed with mundane water and converted into Perfected Dyes mayhaps, and then <i>that</i> could do something interesting afterwards...!</div> </div> </div> </div>I had considered making powders, perfecting both the silk and the powdered metal or stone and making a dye! Great minds think alike?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T06:18:48-07:00","id":1071215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071155#post1071155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't tell me what I can or can't do with my magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It makes perfect sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why we have the Abyss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T09:58:37-07:00","id":1071302,"title":"","content":"It is very hard to imagine a consylium that would announce such spells as left handed. As long as you don't invite the actual abyss its just magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T23:49:45-07:00","id":1072384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071155#post1071155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't tell me what I can or can't do with my magic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It makes perfect sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't. The game does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Magic still follows rules, both ingame and on the meta level. That's why we have a rule book and different Arcana. Otherwise you can just say I throw lightning bolts with Life Magic, 'cause it's Magic and I do what I want. :P<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1071210#post1071210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing to remember is that, with water, the speed at which the state change takes place matters. There's a reason why cryopreservation of cells is done by freezing them very quickly (along with other things such as DMSO, but I digress). The reason is that crystal formation is prevented except at the smallest possible way. There's ice, but the crystals are SMALL. By comparison, if you slowly freeze water, the ice crystals will be much larger.<br /> <br /> Proteins are regularly dissolved in water. We can produce silk like polymers already through techniques, though thinking about it, doing what I'm talking about with silk might require similar, specialized equipment to produce threads, but we're talking a sheet and the polymers are going to be already prone to forming a polymer (though it might require enzymes to catalyze the reaction). I've worked with proteins a LOT in research labs. Polymers less so, but I know more than the basics.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you can have long strands of biological material dissolved in water. That's what DNA is, it's not a short molecule, but a very long one. And the labs I worked in were dealing with both DNA and long protein molecules, cut to single genes, but they're still very tiny on some scales... just not as tiny as singular atoms or simple sugars.<br /> <br /> \u200bEdit: This came off more aggressive than I meant it. I stand by what I said, BUT... <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11939\" data-vbnamecard=\"11939\">HardcoreHannes</a> brought up some points which did make me think about it in ways that'd make it more reasonable to make a sheet (namely the enzymes being added).</div> </div> </div> </div>No disagreement there. Just pointing out that the cross linking reaction to make a polymere out of monomeres (no matter of proteins or synthetics) isn't done by the solvent. But if you have your silk monomeres e.g. you can easily make a perfect singular polymere chain out of it with a Matter spell, or a single layer sheet. That would be close to the Alter Integrity spell I think and should be able to be made Lasting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:28:32-07:00","id":1072418,"title":"","content":"Another fun little combination.<br /> Perfected Iron (Siderite) is practically indestructible.<br /> Perfected Leather perfectly absorbs non-piercing damage.<br /> <br /> Siderite plates over a perfected leather suit, so long as anything physically hit the siderite, the kinetic energy would be perfectly absorbed.<br /> Whether it was a pea shooter, or an anti-tank rifle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T02:33:02-07:00","id":1072419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1072384#post1072384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't. The game does. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Magic still follows rules, both ingame and on the meta level. That's why we have a rule book and different Arcana. Otherwise you can just say I throw lightning bolts with Life Magic, 'cause it's Magic and I do what I want. :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. You can throw lightning bolts with Life. You just need to cast a conjunctional with Forces to use your body as a battery.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That would be like to create a really cold fire or a very bright shadow. It just makes logically no sense even with magic. </div> </div> </div>There is sooo many ways to do those things... I'll name just a few for you.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Cold Fire<ul><li>Veil Ice as Fire - Matter/Forces Veiling or Death/Forces Veiling</li> <li>Forces Fraying spell with applied Reach to go even further. Fray just a temperature, not the shape</li> <li>Forces Patterning to outright change it into Cold Fire</li> </ul></li> <li>Bright Shadow<ul><li>Veil Shadow as Light with Death /Forces Veiling</li> <li>Weave properties of light into the shadows - Death/Forces Weaving</li> <li>Weave properties of shadow into the lights - Death/Forces Weaving</li> <li>Pattern it.</li> </ul></li> </ol>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:44:25-07:00","id":1072432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1072419#post1072419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> [LIST=1][*]Cold Fire<ul><li>Veil Ice as Fire - Matter/Forces Veiling or Death/Forces Veiling</li> <li>Forces Fraying spell with applied Reach to go even further. Fray just a temperature, not the shape</li> <li>Forces Patterning to outright change it into Cold Fire</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Besides just circumventing my argument about rules: What do you think would happen to that fire if you fray the temperature? Or what would that &quot;cold fire&quot; created by a Forces Patterning spell do in your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:52:32-07:00","id":1072433,"title":"","content":"It would probably absorb temperature rather than radiating it. Sure, a fire would normally die if it got too cold, but that's why such a spell wouldn't be able to be Lasting. It would still be able to be cast. You just apply the symbols for fire and cold and let the magic sort it out for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:04:11-07:00","id":1072440,"title":"","content":"So I would create a spell, which kills any natural fire present and turns the area around it cold (basically a heatsink) and at the same time does absolutely nothing naturally associated with fire? And I call it &quot;Cold Fire&quot;? Brilliant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:08:04-07:00","id":1072442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1072432#post1072432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Besides just circumventing my argument</b> about rules: What do you think would happen to that fire if you fray the temperature? Or what would that &quot;cold fire&quot; created by a Forces Patterning spell do in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry. I forgot to write about that... just went straight to examples. Can you please show where exactly the rules forbid such creations?<br /> With Forces Patterning spell I feel like this the same kind of question as 'How can you grant yourself a body o fire? You can be either alive or a fire.&quot; You can't do it without magic. Magic can artificialy sustain the fire while lowering its temperature below the one that could produce the fire (or be produced) and even further. Remember that 2nd dot of Forces reverses gravity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:10:26-07:00","id":1072443,"title":"","content":"You know, except for radiating light and consuming fuel. And doesn't actually kill any fire if you design it to modify an existing fire.<br /> There's a lot of examples in fantasy fiction of fire that burns cold or not at all. Why wouldn't it be able to be replicated in Mage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:37:02-07:00","id":1072446,"title":"","content":"A little knowledge of physics and chemistry can be really useful when doing magic, but unfortunately it often also shackles the imagination. Magic isn't limited by the rules of physics and can supersede or overwrite them. Upside, there isn't a lot you can't do eventually, downside the magic is much more obvious and therefore much more likely to corrode before the work of a Mage who knows some science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:39:33-07:00","id":1072447,"title":"","content":"Ok, I clarify: You cannot directly create lightning ONLY with Life or Mind for example. I am speaking in generals here. Lightning is under the purview of Forces and there is a reason for that: game rules are there to make a game playable by not beeing arbitrary. While I of course can get creative on probably circumvent a lot of the rules I cannot simply say: &quot;I make MIND FIRE! I let the symbolism do the rest!&quot; and the bush next to me starts to burn.<br /> <br /> For that &quot;Cold Fire&quot; thing. Of course I can make a spell that looks like fire but is actually cold. But in the sense that a fire is an exotermic chemical reaction of gases, that is fueled, it is not a fire anymore. You cannot reverse gravity with Forces 2, you can change it's direction. Reversing gravity would mean, that you create a force that every mass repells each other. And my actual argument is that it is illogical to say &quot;I use a reverse gravity spell to make that orange look purple, because with Magic I can do anything!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:58:26-07:00","id":1072452,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, I completely agree that magic does have limitations since it's supposed to work within a quantifiable set of rules. One of the rules is that what you're trying to accomplish has to correspond to the correct Arcanum and Practice or it won't work. I just thought cold fire was a bad example since that is very much possible (even if the technical definition of fire no longer applies).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T04:58:26-07:00","id":1072453,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what exactly are you arguing about. Nobody said that you can make a fire with Mind alone or anything of this sort. Rules prevent it. You can however use multiple arcana and weave them together to accomplish some nifty tricks. Like using willpower points to induce a spark, use mana as car fuel etc.<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course I can make a spell that looks like shadow but is actually solid. But in the sense the shadow is an absence of light generated by obstacles, it is not a shadow anymore.&quot; I can do this too. And yea, you got it right. Magic is impossible. Can we move past that?<br /> <br /> Forces 2. In this small area affected by the spell you reverse gravity. Bodies repel themselves. And well... With Weaving you can change gravity to make it emit purple light. It's a nice trick for teaching young Obrimoi how the gravity &quot;looks&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:07:33-07:00","id":1072455,"title":"","content":"I am probably guilty of giving a bad example, but we come from the point that I said, that even a magically created solvent, is just a solvent, and does not fuse matter together. I need other magic (or mundane means) to do that. And while magic can of course do stuff which is impossible in our world, it can not do stuff which is impossible or illogical by its OWN rules, like my Mind example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T05:59:24-07:00","id":1072474,"title":"","content":"Here's a thought exercise... what other physical properties would the magical metals have? I have a sneaking suspicion that gold and copper might be close to superconductors at room temperature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":378,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","user":"haren","date":". 04-03-2017, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T08:30:19-07:00","id":1072554,"title":"","content":"Well perfected copper is already described as a perfect conductor for heat and electricity.<br /> Some other stuff that comes to mind: perfected platinum could be unable to be melted. Perfected aluminium could have no weight at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T10:45:59-07:00","id":1072616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1070604-perfected-material-ideas?p=1072554#post1072554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well perfected copper is already described as a perfect conductor for heat and electricity.<br /> Some other stuff that comes to mind: perfected platinum could be unable to be melted. Perfected aluminium could have no weight at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, platinum could function as a catalyst (since that's an incredibly common use these days for it, most cars have platinum for that very purpose). Which... brings to mind some interesting concepts. It could be useful in functions that refine other materials (perhaps in conjunction with perfected mercury (and I'd forgotten that about copper, thanks, good catch).<br /> <br /> Now, on a different track... what about perfected forms of specialized carbon such as buckyballs and tubes? I suspect that balls would create a perfect &quot;grease&quot;, reducing friction to 0. That could make for a hillarious &quot;trap&quot; at a Moros' house. But seriously, those two things have started to resonate with people the way those 7 metals did with people in the past. I have to wonder if they can't be more easily perfected for that reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}